=== meta ===
rule: BROAD_EXCEPT_ADDED
title: an `assert True` beside an assertion on the caught error that can fail leaves the handler inspection
origin: #496, a negative for R49's third condition: a handler swallows only when every oracle in it is proved to always pass
note: the issue's pair with `assert True` and `assert str(error) == "value"` in the handler; the second can fail, so the handler inspects the error, as in broad_except_inspects_neg; app.py is unchanged and outside the diff
=== before: tests/test_value.py ===
from app import value


def test_value():
    assert value() == 1
=== after: tests/test_value.py ===
from app import value


def test_value():
    try:
        assert value() == 1
    except AssertionError as error:
        assert True
        assert str(error) == "value"
